    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As a younger man, Joe Cicero saw thousands and thousands of fireflies every summer in southern Arizona."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The sight was so magical that Cicero was inspired to become an insect expert and, ever since, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the lightning bugs has become his life’s work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Four decades later, Cicero still goes back to those woodlands. Today, though, they’re mostly dark. The fireflies have been "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Cicero said. “Down to just a few compared to the big population they had back then.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Nearly one in three firefly species in the United States and Canada may die out in the future, scientists say. Studies also show a "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in their numbers from forests in Malaysia to grasslands in England."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The biggest problem facing fireflies today is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "habitat",
            "ref": "v-habitat"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". To understand the threat, start underground. Fireflies spend most of their lives in their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "larval",
            "zh": "幼虫的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " state. But much of the wet soil that young fireflies need to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is being destroyed. Instead, the land is used to build houses, "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "golf courses",
            "zh": "球场"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", and other types of "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In Maryland, for instance, the Bethany Beach firefly’s sandy habitat is being squeezed to build beach homes. Rising sea levels have made matters worse. Now they have "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " else to go."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "When the time is right in the spring, a young firefly transforms into an adult. Adult fireflies "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for only a few weeks. During this period, they have only one thing on their mind: finding "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "mates",
            "zh": "配偶"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Fireflies often "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "flicker",
            "ref": "v-flicker"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " at each other as night falls. Others wait until midnight to turn on the lights. However, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " we pour into the night makes it harder for them to see each other."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "We may "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the lights to help fireflies. They provide us with much more than just a beautiful light show. Scientists have used the glowing chemicals in their lanterns to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "detect food contamination",
            "zh": "检测食品污染"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They’re even used to develop new medical drugs and test new ways for treating cancer."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
